## Key Takeaways

- Docker Networking enables container communication and controlled access.
- User-defined bridge networks support container-name DNS resolution.
- Port publishing exposes a container port through a host port.
- Host, None, Container, and Overlay modes have different purposes and limitations.
- Inspect networks, check application ports, and read logs when troubleshooting.

